XSTRATEGIES OF HACK:
X
XIt's hard to give specific spoilers since I don't know what you may need
Xto improve upon, but at least I can tell you what works for me. My track
Xrecord is ~50% wins for all games (~25% wins if the character is Healer).
X
XFirst, can I assume we're talking about Nethack? If not, perhaps a subset
Xof the following will apply. I only play V2.2, the strategies may vary
Xfor V2.3 .
X
XThe game is played in stages, with different goals and strategies at each
Xstage. Here is a brief rundown:
X
X1. Getting Started - Escaping the Orcs
X
XYou must reach at least experience level 3 (25 or more HP) before you go
Xdown very far in the dungeon. I usually stay on Levels 1-2 until I reach
Xthis point. I always leave the dog on Level 1 unless I run into a bunch
Xof Orcs on Level 2, in which case I use him to run interference while I
Xdash to the '>' down to Level 3. Orcs are the most difficult monster
Xyou have to deal with at this stage. You should avoid prolonged fights
Xwith them until your armor is 2 or lower. When you are ready to take
Xthem on, pick your battlefield carefully. You should have a clear path
Xto a staircase. Don't let them circle and block your retreat. Get them
Xto chase you down a corridor where you can turn a corner and fight them
Xone at a time without taking darts from the Orcs in the rear. If you
Xhave a 'hit at a distance' wand, you may want to fire it at them down a
Xstraight hallway to take out several at once. If you find your hit points
Xgetting low, beat a hasty retreat to the stairs. You can always wait on
Xanother level to regenerate and come back to finish the fight later. Once
Xyou have the Orcs under control, you are ready for the next stage.
X
X2. Identifying Magic Items - Beating the killer bees
X
XDon't read any scrolls until you have more than you can carry. This is
Xusually around Level 7 or lower. Dump all your scrolls, spellbooks and
Xspare items by the '>', then go to lower levels and bring back all the
Xscrolls you find there. The idea is to get as many scrolls as possible.
XKeep going down until you run into something really nasty like a killer
Xbee or Dragon, then quickly retreat to your scroll pile. Be systematic
Xin the way you identify scrolls. Wear expendable armor until you find
X'destroy armor'. Wield an expendable weapon after you find 'enchant
Xweapon'. Read those scrolls which you have the most copies of first.
XUsually 'identify', 'light', and 'teleportation' are the most numerous.
XUse 'identify' scrolls to identify rings first. After that, use them
Xto identify other scrolls. Don't enchant armor beyond +4; don't enchant
Xweapons beyond +5 (identify the weapon if that is likely). Genocide
Xmonsters in this order: Dragon, cockatrice (if new moon), xan/killer
Xbee (depending on armor). Once you have identified all, or almost all
Xscrolls, you will hopefully be ready to take on the killer bees. You
Xmust first gain poison immunity, which means eating a spider or killer
Xbee, then retreating until you recover your strength. Your armor must
Xbe at least -1, and you should wield at least a +1 katana, two-handed
Xsword, long sword, or chrysknife. Fight the bees with the same tactics
Xused on the Orcs, and use every advantage you have - speed, wands,
Xspells, etc. Once you get past the bees, it's on to the next stage.
X
X3. Fire Resistance - Beating Dragons
X
XIf you have genocided Dragons, then you just need to max out your luck
Xand let the gods give you fire resistence for the fires of hell. If
XD's are still a menace, then you must find, kill, and eat one in order
Xto survive this stage. When you locate a Dragon, stash all your scrolls
Xand potions in a safe place and find a long, narrow room in which to do
Xbattle. The idea is to lure the Dragon into the room where you can
Xeither sleep it or outrun it while you attack. Sleeping is the best
Xidea; then you are usually free to hit it from a distance with wands,
Xspells or weapons until it dies. If you have to fight hand to hand,
Xyou had better haste yourself/slow the Dragon so you can hit and move
Xback out of its line of fire. If your armor is at least -2, and your
Xweapon is at least +2, and your HP is > 100, you'll probably survive.
XIf not, you'd better bypass Dragon levels until you get your stats up.
X
X4. Improving Your Luck - Beating Medusa
X
XYou need to increase your luck to maximum by throwing gems at unicorns.
XBy the time you find your first unicorn you will probably have at least
Xten unidentified gems, so you just need to get it to hold still long
Xenough to shower it with gifts. You can sleep or slow unicorns and make
Xit very easy to catch up with them. If you have intrinsic teleport and
Xteleport control, you can corner them and move next to them on an
X'automatic' teleport (not ^T). If all else fails, just keep chasing
Xthem until you get your chance. With each gift, they lose some of
Xtheir shyness. After ten unidentified gems, you will have maximized
Xyour luck, and wonderful things start happening when you pray, sit on
Xthrones, drink from fountains, etc. With or without the unicorn's
Xhelp, it is relatively easy to get by the Medusa. She usually resides
Xon Level 26 or 27. It's best to do monster detection when you first
Xreach Level 25. Once you find the Medusa, you can either kill her or
Xbypass her level (level teleport or dig a hole in the floor) to get
Xto the first maze level with its guaranteed wand of wishing. To kill
Xthe Medusa, you must first blind yourself (potion of blindness or
Xblindfold), then apply the mirror to her, zap her, or beat on her
X(only if you have quaffed blindness). She usually stays by the '>'
Xuntil something wakens her.
X
X5. Getting the Amulet - Beating the Wizard
X
XYou will find a wand of wishing under an enormous boulder in a cul-
Xde-sac on the first maze level. Get at it either by digging a hole
Xin the wall and pushing the boulder aside, dropping everything else
Xand squeezing in to get it, or by hitting it with the pickaxe. Use
Xthe wand to wish for any of the following items missing from your
Xinventory: ring of teleport control (you need intrinsic teleport
Xability), ring of polymorph control (so you don't hose your armor
Xon the first polymorph trap), blindfold (so you don't have to search
Xevery maze level for the wizard), +3 crystal plate mail (the best
Xfor its weight), +3 elven cloak (you probably didn't get this far
Xwithout one), wand of polymorph (if you want to play the polymorph
Xpile game), 3 scrolls of enchantment (if you want to boost your
Xarmor or weapon strength), 3 dilithium crystals (so you will know
Xthe most valuable gemstone when you see it). Now you can either
Xspend time gathering up valuables to escape the dungeon with or go
Xright for the Wizard and his Amulet. Assuming it's the latter,
Xlevel teleport yourself down to Level 60 (ring of teleport control,
Xpotion of confusion or booze, scroll of teleportation, or level
Xteleport trap), and search for the '<'. Once you find it, put on
Xyour blindfold and start ascending stairs (they're all connecting).
XEventually, usually between Levels 35-45, you will find the 'd1' pair.
XRemove the blindfold and clear a path to the Wizard's castle.
XThe castle is surrounded by a moat which you will either need to fill
Xwith an enormous boulder, vaporize with fire, or levitate across.
XThe castle wall may be breeched with a pick-axe or other digging
Ximplement - there's a minotaur on every level who carries a wand
Xof digging. Kill the Wizard's dog, get the Amulet, and either
Xkill or ignore the Wizard, as you please. I believe he's less
Xtrouble if you kill him immediately, although he keeps rising
Xfrom the dead. You are free to simply walk out of the dungeon
Xat this point, although the Wizard may put various obstacles in
Xyour path. Level teleporting is greatly impaired by the Amulet,
Xbut if you have enough teleportation scrolls, it is possible to
Xteleport directly to Level 1. I have never had any trouble
Xescaping the dungeon once I reached the point where I was capable
Xof getting the Amulet.
