XOVERALL STRATEGIES:
X
XThe following is is a discussion of the various strategies used by
Xhack players, and some helpful advice from Erik Lauer, our resident hack
Xexpert.
X
XThe blitz strategy:
X
XThis strategy is to blitz down as far as possible, taking only enough
Xtime to find the items on the level and collect them. This particular
Xstrategy is usually used by more inexperienced players who want to see how
Xfar they can get in a certain amount of time. In fact, it is surprisingly
Xeasy to go down levels, at least to the 26th level, even with a character
Xtaken to ensure this does not happen.
X
XThe "snail's pace" strategy:
X
XHere the player will only go down when he is running low on food. This
Xallows the player to develop as much as possible before encountering the
Xharder creatures on the next level. This strategy has a few intrinsic problems.
XOne is that it is extremely easy to run too low on food if the player is not
Xcareful. Another is that this takes a very long time, and so is only for the
Xtruly patient. Finally, there is a point of diminishing returns, sometime
Xaround when the cockatrices first appear, that it is no longer profitable to
Xfudge around on the upper levels.
X
XThe best overall strategy is somewhere in between the two, and is based
Xprimarily on what you find available.
X
XAlthough overall strategy is important, the most important thing in hack
Xis based on a simple idea: Hack is a game for opportunists.
X
XThat is, as hack has grown, and more options become available to the
Xplayer, every little detail presents a potential tool for the observant
Xplayer. This has become increasingly true as hack expanded into nethack.
X
XTry to find a use for everything you find. I read an article once in
Xwhich the writer denounced the destroy armor scroll as totally worthless.
XHe had never thought that he could use it to destroy cursed armor also,
Xand so made his game that much harder.
X
XIf you can do this, then you can win the game.
X
XSPECIFIC HINTS ON VARIOUS PARTS OF HACK:
X
XStores:
X
XThis section presents probably the most useful thing in hack: the
Xstore. The secret to stores does not lie in the buying of items, however.
XThe real secret lies in robbing them blind.
X
XThere are probably as many ways to steal from shops as there are
Xshopkeepers. The most common is to acquire teleportation, on a scroll, wand,
Xor intrinsically, pick up everything you can in the shop, and teleport out.
XAnother method is to polymorph the shopkeeper. He may become more powerful,
Xbut it is not very likely. You can then walk past him. Another possibility
Xis to kill the shopkeeper. This is recommended only if you are powerful
X(shopkeepers are not wimps), and either desperate or just plain sadistic.
XFinally, you can steal individual items by having your dog go into the shop
Xand bring them out. Reward your dog after he brings you the first item,
Xand he will continue bringing you items. Any item on the space directly
Xin front of the door is a freebie.
X
XTeleportation is the best method by far. Since it is very to find a
Xleprechaun on the first and second levels, it is highly recommended that
Xyou eat one, and thereby gain intrinsic teleportation. The same in fact goes
Xfor finding floating eyes to gain telepathy.
X
XKops:
X
XThe Keystone Kops were an addition to nethack, originally intended to
Xhinder people who rob shops. When a shop is robbed, a number of "K"'s appear.
XThe Kops attack by throwing cream pies at you, and regenerate when they are
Xkilled.
X
XHowever, the Kops in fact represent yet another aspect of hack which
Xthe observant player can make excellent use of. The Kops are very easy to
Xkill, and do very little damage. Although you can be blinded by a cream pie,
Xsince it is very easy to acquire telepathy, this is definitely not a
Xhindrance. Most importantly, since every Kop carries a large number of
Xcream pies, they also create an abundance of readily available food. Finally,
Xsince Kops sometimes carry magic items, killing them gives the user hoards
Xof treasure. Regeneration is, therefore, just a bonus, because it means
Xyour supplies of food, treasure and experience points will not run out.
X
XThere is only one way the Kops can hurt a player who is even moderately
Xpowerful, but it should not be taken lightly. If the Kops throw a cream pie
Xat you, but miss and hit the shopkeeper, the shopkeeper will get mad and
Xattack you. This means that you must trap the shopkeeper if you do not
Xwant him getting in the way. The best way is to trap yourself and the
Xshopkeeper with a boulder in the shop. Then, when you teleport out, the
Xshopkeeper is alive, but trapped.
X
XFood:
X
XOnce you have mastered combat, you will find that food becomes the
Xmain problem. If you do not continually eat food, you will eventually begin
Xto faint and starve. Fainting is often enough to kill a character by itself.
X
XThe key is to hunt down food constantly. Hunt, kill and eat all the
Xedible creatures you can find. ALWAYS search for monsters which can give
Xyou special abilities. In particular, before continuing below the second
Xlevel you should find and eat, if possible, a leprechaun and a floating
Xeye. See my earlier comment on eating leprechauns.
X
XHowever, do not eat so much that you could not eat any more. The
Xreason is that if you are on the verge of choking, and kill, for example,
Xa wraith, you would not be able to eat the cadaver for a long time, and so
Xit might spoil before you get the chance.
X
XUnidentified items:
X
XYet another key point is to find out as quickly as possible which
Xitems have which powers. This does not mean, however, that you should
Xtry every item out the instant you get it.
X
XWe will deal with the different items separately.
X
XPotions:
X
XYou should almost never test out potions until you are at fith level for
Xwizards, or ninth level for other characters, at full hit points and are on
Xa cleared level. If you are not of those levels, you run the risk of wasting
Xa potion of gain level without gaining the ability to teleport at will.
Xonly if you have teleportitis. If you are not at full hit points, then
Xshould you quaff a healing potion, it will not affect your maximum hit
Xpoints. If there are creatures nearby, you run the risk of being paralyzed
Xor confused, and unable to defend yourself. Lastly, always test your
Xduplicate potions first.
X
XScrolls:
X
XYou should only test out scrolls when you are wearing a spare set of
Xarmor and are wielding a spare weapon. This allows you to not risk your good
Xequipment on determining which scrolls are the destroy armor and damage
Xweapon scrolls. Of course, once one of these have been found, you no longer
Xhave to take precautions against it. You also should wait until you have
Xsomething to identify, in case it is an identify scroll. You won't have to
Xwait long. And, as with potions, check the duplicate scrolls first.
X
XRings:
X
XRings should be identified first, since they are the hardest thing
Xto identify, aside from gems. Trying on unidentified rings is not encouraged,
Xas one cursed ring can ruin the game. If you have a scroll of remove curse,
Xit is safe to try on the ring. You can check it out if there is a Nymph on
Xthe level. That is dealt with later. If you have several unidentified
Xrings, (or armor or weapons) try them all until you have on as many
Xcursed items as possible. This will allow you to de-curse as many as
Xpossible with one scroll.
X
XWands:
X
XALWAYS test out wands as soon as there is a weak monster in your area
Xto zap them at. Since wand might shoot out a ray or a bolt, which bounce,
Xit is vitally important to shoot the wand diagnolly in such a way that
Xshould the bolt bounce, it will not hit the character. The bolt is of a
Xfinite length, so in a large room it may be safely zapped in a straight
Xline. Sometimes this is not a good idea. You might get a polymorph wand
Xand might polymorph that weak monster into a dragon or other powerful
Xmonster.
X
XUsually, the wand's function is now apparent. For wands, however, this
Xmay not be sufficient to identify the wand. After zapping such a wand, and
Xobserving the target, call the wand something such as "tested1". This shows
Xyou that, although its purpose is not known, the wand has been used. If in
XNetHack, you also could try to engrave with the wand. This will identify
Xa lot of wands. The others could be identified by some other means.
XYou can also engrave with the wand, "E". The wands function should then
Xbecome apparent.
X
XSpellbooks:
X
XDo not read spellbooks until you are at least eighth level and have
Xidentified a scroll of amnesia. This is because transcribing spells is hard
Xfor characters less than eighth level, and the amnesia scroll remove all the
Xspells you know. In either case, the user loses valuable spellbooks. If
Xyou know any spells, but don't know which scroll is amnesia, don't read
Xany scroll without identifying it. Also, just because you can learn a
Xspell, doesn't mean you can cast it. Since spellbooks have a limited
Xnumber of castings, be careful not to waste them.
X
XVaults:
X
XEventually, the player will encounter what is known as a treasure
Xvault. The vault is a 2x2 room, with four "$" spaces, and no doors. There
Xis always a secret door somewhere on a vault level which leads to a space
Xwhich teleports the user to the vault. There is always an engraving which
Xsays "ad ?ae??um." If you find this engraving, search for the secret door
Xnext to it.
X
XTo get out of a vault with all the money, you have to either teleport
Xor use a wand of digging. If you have neither, eventually a guard will
Xenter the vault. He is harmless, but will lead you out of the vault if you
Xare carrying NO money. Should you discover the answer to his question, he
Xwill leave by yourself in the vault. (In other words, knowing the answer
Xdoes not help). My luckiest move was zapping a guard with a wand of
Xpolymorph. He turned into a Quantum Mechanic, hit me, and teleported me out.
X
XNymphs:
X
XAlthough Nymphs can be annoying, they can do one extremely useful
Xthing: they can steal cursed items. Therefore, if a Nymph is found, you
Xcan use her to remove your cursed items. The way this is done is demonstrated
Xin the following example of how to check unidentified rings with a Nymph on
Xthe level.
X
X1) Clear out the level the Nymph is on.
X2) Go down to the next level, and clear it.
X3) Try putting on your unidentified rings. If a ring is not cursed,
X   name it something such as "uncursed1" to mark that this
X   type of ring is not cursed.
X4) Upon finding a cursed ring, remove ALL of your equipment, and drop
X   it on that space. Then go up the stairs, find the Nymph, and
X   let her steal an item. The item she steals then has to be
X   the cursed item. Go back down, equip yourself, and continue.
X
XNot using the dog:
X
XAlthough the dog seems to be a useful ally, in fact he presents a good
Xplayer with a handicap. This is for a number of reasons.
X1) Anything the dog kills, the character does not get experience for.
X   This means that it takes longer to go up levels while using the dog.
X2) The dog will eat edible monsters and other Comestibles that the
X   character needs. Hence, there is less food for the character.
X3) Perhaps the worst thing about the dog is that the user can NOT enter
X   the dog's space. This means that the dog can actually trap the user
X   in a corridor, and prevent the user's escape from a powerful monster.
XFor these reasons, unless you have the uncontrollable urge to experiment with
Xthe dog, it is best to leave the dog behind on the first level.
X
XCarry extra items, but don't carry gold:
X
XThe user should always carry as many items as he possibly can through
Xthe dungeon. This is because even worthless items can be polymorphed or sold
Xin the shops for gold. On the other hand, you should NEVER carry gold. The
Xgold weighs a non-negligible amount, and is not used unless the person is
Xbuying an item in a shop. Since buying items is very rare, it is best to
Xpile all the gold from a level next to the stairs going up. That way, on the
Xway back up, the winning player can collect all the money he left behind.
XBut, weight for weight, the most valuable gem is worth many times more than
Xthe gold you could carry around. Bring rocks and polymorph them into gems.
X
XOne useful technique of bringing more items than you can carry along
Xis to shuffle them down. Carry your items in two (or more) piles. Leave one
Xpile by the stairs, while carrying the other items. When you find the stairs
Xgoing down, drop the surplus items, go get the other pile, and bring it down
Xto the next level. Drop that pile, go back up, and get the other items.
XOr you could wear a ring of leviatation and use that to go up the stairs.
X
XFighting floating eyes:
X
XMany beginning players fight floating eyes by killing them in hand
Xto hand combat. This is not a very good method, since it lets the eye get a
Xchance to paralyze you. Instead, it is far preferable to attack floating eyes
Xby throwing weapons at them. If you have your dog, you can always let the dog
Xkill it, and then step in to eat the eye before the dog gets a chance.
X
XKilling Leprechauns:
X
XThe leprechaun is yet another reason not to carry any gold at all. If
Xyou are hit by a leprechaun while you have gold, not only do you lose the
Xgold (temporarily), but the trickster also teleports away, and so you have
Xto hunt him down. If you do not have any gold, however, he is a very weak
Xmonster worth gold and experience. Before you fight one, drop your gold in a
Xplace he can not get to, and then kill him. Also be careful about letting
Xthe leprechaun run away, since he is faster than you are.
X
XDealing with Shapechangers:
X
XOnce you begin to encounter shapechangers, you should already be able
Xto deal with all the other creatures. The shape-changers, however, are the
Xmost potentially dangerous creatures in the game, because they cannot be
Xgenocided and can turn into previously genocided creatures.
