XREAL SPOILERS:
X
XThe following are spoilers which go beyond (in my opinion) helpful hints.
XSome of these spoilers (in fact most of them) can be figured out in the
Xcourse of play, but they also dramatically change how the game works.
XRead this only if you are truly stuck.
X
XELBERETH:
X
XAny version which has engraving has the secret word Elbereth in it.
XIf the user etches the word "Elbereth" on the ground, and does not smudge
Xthe word by moving (you may type "."), monster will flee in terror upon
Xmoving adjacent to the user, so long as the user stands on that space. It
Xworks much like a scare monster scroll, except that the user can not attack
Xoff of it and preserve its abilities.
X
XUsing Elbereth allows a competent player to win at will, but it is
Xbasically cheating. It is possible to guess about the word Elbereth, however.
XUse it only when no one is watching. Elbereth has been weakened as of
Xrelease 2.2 of NetHack. The various denzins of the dungeon can throw stuff
Xat you and other indirect attacks. You have a chance of rubbing out the
XElbereth unless you use a sharp weapon or a Magic Marker.
X
XEXCALIBUR:
X
XIn nethack, there is a fairly good chance that any long sword named
X"Excalibur" will become +5 after being dipped in a fountain. This gives a
Xvery powerful weapon to anyone who can get a long sword; in particular a
Xknight.
X
XCROESUS:
X
XCroesus is the name that the vault guard is expecting. This does not
Xhelp you win the game, but is listed for the curious.
X
XTHE RUBBER CHICKEN ATTACK:
X
XIf the user is wearing gloves, he may pick up and wield a dead
Xcockatrice. Any creature struck by the bird is automatically turned to
Xstone. Unfortunately, the cockatrice disintigrates after a period of time,
Xbut in the mean time it can wreak vast devastation. Be careful! Should
Xyou fall down while carrying a dead cockatrice, it may accidentally
Xtouch you! The cockatrice, though a powerful weapon, is not a good
Xweapon because it turns potential food into stone. Just a warning.
X
XPOLYMORPHING WANDS:
X
XOne really big spoiler is that should you collect a large number of
Xwands (from a wand shop, for example), and put them in a pile, you may
Xpolymorph the wands, and try to get wands of wishing. With enough wands and
Xcharges in your polymorph wand, you can eventually get at least one wand of
Xwishing. By wishing for more polymorph wands, you can continue the process,
Xacquiring a truly disgusting number of wishes. The best part is that the
Xcharges are the charges the old wand had, so that one wand may have up
Xto 15 wishes!! Clearly this presents a simple, yet powerful (and cheap)
Xmethod of winning. This is also the only use I have found for the
Xfabled "wand of nothing." They have a lot of charges.
X
XPOLYMORPHING YOUR DOG:
X
XIf you want a real powerful pet, you can polymorph your dog, and he
Xwill remain loyal to you. However, if you have a large dog, he's
Xprobably just as good without being polymorphed.
X
XPRAYING FOR FOOD:
X
XOne fairly common effect of praying is that the character is surrounded
Xby a strong aura. This aura not only heals damage and restores strength, but
Xit also raises the user's maximum hp. by 5 AND restores the user's hunger to
Xits initial value of 900 turns. This means that, by praying every 300+ turns,
Xeven if this result only occurs once out of every four tries, the amount
Xof food that needs to be eaten is better than halved. Use the time option
Xto keep track of when it is time to pray.
X
XCANCELING WANDS OF WISHING:
X
XIt is an interesting fact that a wand with zero charges CAN be zapped
Xafter a long number of tries, after which it can no longer be zapped, and
Xhas -1 charges. This works for wands of wishing as well. But, a wand of
Xcancellation used on another wand makes the wand have 0 charges. Hence, by
Xzapping a wand of wishing with a wand of cancellation after the wand is at
X-1 charges gives the user another wish. The user can continue this process
Xindefinitely, but it takes a VERY long time. This is really an alternative
Xto the polymorphing technique mentioned previously, but can be used by
Xearlier versions of hack. That's another "feature" written out of NetHack
X2.2. When a wand reaches -1 charges, it disintegrates.
X
XIRON BALLS:
X
XThe punishment scroll gives you an extremely powerful weapon: the
XIron Ball. Although the cockatrice is more powerful, it has the disadvantages
Xof disintegrating and of destroying all edible monster. The iron ball,
Xalthough very heavy, can kill many monsters in one swing, and almost every
Xmonster in two. Try wielding it some time. The authors neglect to
Xmention that you have to get the thing off your ankle. I believe this
Xcan be done via remove curse, or by praying. I know it can be done by
Xpolymorphing yourself into a Nymph and using the #remove command.
X
XNURSES AND THE SPELL OF EXTRA-HEALING:
X
XBoth of these allow the user to gain an enormous number of hp. The
Xspell grants the user hit points each time it is cast, so the user can
Xwith this spell increase his maximum hit points as many times as he has the
Xmana to do it. No longer true, since the spell has a finite number of
Xuses.
X
XNurses will cast extra healing on any character they "attack" which
Xis not wearing any armor. This means that by letting a nurse attack you for
Xa long period of time, you can gain literally hundreds of hit points.
X
XFINDING THE WANDS OF WISHING ON THE 26TH LEVEL AND BELOW:
X
XEach level below the 25th has a wand of wishing on it. The wands are
Xlocated beneath a large boulder ("`") which is adjacent to 3 walls. To get
Xone of the wands, use a wand of digging to create a hole next to the boulder
Xand push the boulder away. Using a wand of striking will work also. You
Xcan also remove most of your goodies, and move toward the rock again.
XThis will let you crawl under it to get the wand.
X
XTHE MEDUSA:
X
XA new creature, the medusa, has been added as of NetHack 2.2. She is
Xa unique monster, shown by the symbol "8". She guards the lower levels,
Xand can be tough to defeat, since looking at her will instantly turn you
Xto stone. Two items have been added to help you: the mirror, and the
Xblindfold. Using these is the most popular method of destroying the medusa,
Xbut there are others. You can blind yourself with a camera or quaff a
Xpotion of blindness and attack her.
X
XGOING BELOW THE 26TH LEVEL:
X
XTo go below the 26th level, you must be confused and read a teleport
Xscroll with a ring of teleport control on. This allows you to teleport to a
Xlower level. The dungeon goes down to the 40th level, and none of the levels
Xbeyond the 26th have stairs going down. 40 is no longer the lowest
Xlevel, and the Wizard isn't always there.
X
XSURVIVING THE 40TH LEVEL.
X
XYou MUST have fire resistance to enter the 40th level and live. The
Xamulet is guarded by a powerful wizard and his hell hound. They are located
Xin the center of the level, surrounded by a moat, and an inner wall.
XIt looks like this:
X
X ~~~~~~
X ~----~
X ~|..|~
X ~----~
X ~~~~~~
XThe wizard is located in the center. You can levitate over the water, or you
Xcan destroy a space of water with a wand of fire. Once over the water, use
Xa wand of digging to blast open the wall, fight the wizard and retrieve the
Xamulet. Now leave the dungeon, and collect as much money as you can.
XYou also get bonus points for leaving with a pet. These points are directly
Xrelated to the pet's experience level.
